From 8d0509b65201c3173e96b813975ba0008cec333f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:51:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] ants3: GDML export names for materials and post-export
 check

Add AMaterialHub::makeGdmlExportName(iMat, name), which builds the name
a material gets in the GDML file exported for g4ants3:
"m<iMat>_<sanitized name>". The sanitizer is an allow-list
([A-Za-z0-9_.-], everything else -> '_') so ROOT's TGDMLWrite::GenName
(private, cannot be reused) has nothing to change. "0x" is broken up
because Geant4's G4GDMLRead::StripName truncates names there, and
"_refl" because ROOT removes it.

AGeometryHub::exportGeometry gets a forG4ants3 flag. When set, the
export pass creates the TGeoMaterials with the export names, and after
export the GDML file is read back (QXmlStreamReader) to check that
every expected material name is present exactly once. If ROOT ever
changes its naming rules, the export fails with an explicit error
instead of silently producing mismatched names.

The flag defaults to false, so this commit changes no behaviour; the
g4ants3 export switches to it in the next commit together with the new
material transfer format.

